      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your articulation of feeling shredded by expectations is profound, and I hear the longing for true agency in it. While the feeling that control is an illusion is very common, there are many documented versions of reality where people reclaim ownership over their daily choices and relationships. The idea that being \"your own master\" is a fairy tale might be a defense mechanism against the crushing weight of your current experience, but it ignores the countless small acts of self-preservation people use daily to carve out space for themselves. Please consider that these feelings stem from real human pain rather than a logical conclusion that you are powerless.",
      "source": "target",
